    "body": "Triage: `bug`, `P1`, `area:turning` (cross drilling on lathe/mill-turn). Human-filed, so no `source:agent`.\n\nBoth tests pass on Windows: the batch gate on main at 5accdd5 passed all 966 app tests, `drilling_cross_box` and `drilling_cross_spindle` included. Nothing that touches these suites has merged since then (cac115a only adds docs and the Heidenhain extension). That points to platform float sensitivity on macOS/aarch64, not a regression on main.\n\nNot P2, though: test 2 says the lathe chain gets one more move when only the work offset moves. If that's float-dependent, the NC output depends on the platform and the G54 position, which is wrong output, not just a stale golden. Next step: reproduce on Linux x86_64, then find which move the extra one is (likely a tolerance-edge split or dedupe in the cross-drill chain) and make it offset-invariant. The fingerprint test should compare with a tolerance instead of hashing raw float bits.",
